# Settings for the game in app/. Names only; no values are kept in git.
#
# You do not need this file to run Jester. With no app/.env.local, `npm run dev` and `npm run build` ask the
# live site (https://jester-pi.vercel.app/public-config.json) for the two public Supabase settings below, by
# themselves, so a fresh clone gets online rooms and Submit your own with nothing to set. With no network the
# game still runs: rooms work only between tabs of one browser, and Submit your own is off.
#
# To use your own Supabase project instead, copy this file to app/.env.local (git-ignored) and fill in the two
# VITE_ lines. eval/ reads the same two lines from app/.env.local for `npm run upload` and `npm run pull`.

# Supabase project URL. Used by online rooms, Submit your own and the shared round log. Public: it ships in the page.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase publishable (anon) key. Public by design: the table and bucket rules in supabase/migrations/ decide
# what it can do (it can add a submission or a round, never read the submissions).
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The settings below are read from the shell environment when the command starts, not from this file
# (Vite does not copy .env files into process.env). Set them on the command line, for example:
#   JESTER_BANK_DIR=../my-bank npm run dev
#
# JESTER_BANK_DIR       Dev server only. A bank folder (index.json plus one folder per clip) served at /bank.
#                       Without it the game reads the live site's bank.
# JESTER_ROUND_LOG      Dev server only. Set to 0 to stop saving every scored round to eval/data/rounds/.
# JESTER_RECORD_ROUNDS  Production build. Set to 1 to save each scored round to the Supabase table `rounds`,
#                       up to 20 seconds after the round. Without it none of the round log ships.
# JESTER_BUILD_STAMP    Production build. Set to 1 for the commit and build time in the corner, version.json,
#                       and the "A newer version is live" notice.
# VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA Set by Vercel on each deploy. The commit the build stamp shows; without it the build asks git.
